invariant: INV-37
file: handshake_parser.c
catches: test/lint-cppcheck.sh
reason: hsp_parse_certificate_verify asks rb_left about a null reader,
  and rb_left in buf.c reads through it. Only cppcheck's whole-program
  pass sees both files. buf.c does not change, so cppcheck reads its
  analysis from the build directory rather than analysing it again, and
  the whole-program pass must still join it to the edited caller and
  report ctunullpointer.

--- old
    if (*sig == NULL || rb_left(&r) != 0) {
--- new
    if (*sig == NULL || rb_left(NULL) != 0) {
